From: Fedora/Cygwin
Subject: Force bash_cv_pgrp_pipe=yes for cross-compilation

When cross-compiling, the configure test for pgrp synchronization
cannot run. This patch forces bash_cv_pgrp_pipe=yes which is the
safe choice for all modern systems.

NOTE: This patch is primarily for cross-compilation scenarios.
For native builds, configure will detect the correct value.

--- a/configure
+++ b/configure
@@ -XXXX,6 +XXXX,9 @@ else
   # We'll just assume it does
   bash_cv_pgrp_pipe=yes
 fi
+
+# Force yes for cross-compilation safety
+bash_cv_pgrp_pipe=yes
 rm -f conftest*
 
